{"accepted_at":"2026-09-05T03:22:24Z","case":{"argument_date":"2024-01-17T00:00:00Z","arguments":[{"argument_date":"2024-01-17T00:00:00Z","heading":"What happened at the argument","official_detail_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcript/2023","official_transcript_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-1219_4246.pdf","paragraphs":["Relentless claims Chevron distorts the judicial process. It asserts the doctrine undermines statutory interpretation.","The government claims Chevron has deep roots in jurisprudence. It argues the sides that brought the case lack extraordinary justification to overrule it.","Justice Thomas questioned the line between deference and judicial duty. He referenced Skidmore deference in his inquiry.","Chief Justice Roberts explored fact-bound interstate commerce scenarios. He asked if agency policy judgment remains pertinent there."],"reargument":false,"sequence":1,"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 10, lines 25-27","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-1219_4246.pdf","page_label":"file page 10, lines 25-27"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 10, lines 9-21","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-1219_4246.pdf","page_label":"file page 10, lines 9-21"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 11, lines 11-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-1219_4246.pdf","page_label":"file page 11, lines 11-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 12, lines 11-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-1219_4246.pdf","page_label":"file page 12, lines 11-19"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript",